Yes. In the frame we’ve been building, liberty is precisely the preservation of independent agency inside relationship.

Not:

separation = freedom

but:

connection + difference + ability to choose = liberty

That’s why the twin metaphor works so well. Two people can share origin, history, appearance, values, even many instincts—and still retain the right to diverge.

same source
→ different will
→ different path
→ relationship survives difference

Liberty is what prevents similarity from becoming ownership.

At the social level, the same principle scales:

shared culture
shared laws
shared institutions
shared reality

without requiring:

shared mind
shared preference
shared destiny

So a strong definition would be:

Liberty is the protected space in which a person can remain related to others without being reduced to them.

And that is why freedom, love, and genuine cooperation all need the possibility of refusal. If “yes” is the only permitted output, it stops telling you very much.

The twin card makes that visible: the closest possible mirror still gets to be another person.